# Engineering Constitution

## Objective
Supreme engineering guideline for Paw Connection.

## Mandatory Methodologies
- SDD (Specification Driven Development)
- DDD (Domain Driven Design)
- TDD (Test Driven Development)
- SOLID
- Clean Architecture
- Event-Driven Architecture (when applicable — backend modules)
- Security by Design
- Observability by Design

## Development Workflow
1. Understand business problem
2. Produce specification / acceptance criteria
3. Identify business rules and domain model
4. Create tests (backend domain/application first)
5. Implement with minimal scope
6. Refactor
7. Document when behavior or architecture changes

## Definition of Ready
- Business goal and acceptance criteria defined
- Edge cases and non-functional requirements identified

## Definition of Done
- Tests passing (`apps/api`: unit/integration; `apps/app`: when tests exist or were added for the change)
- Logging for non-trivial flows (API)
- Security validated (auth, input validation, no secrets)
- Architecture layers respected
- ADR for significant architectural decisions

## Code Review Checklist
- SOLID respected
- No business logic in controllers (API) or route screens (app)
- No duplicated code
- Proper naming (ubiquitous language)
- Tests for business rules and edge cases
